      "writtenOn": "2023-11-09T15:45:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why do some use `hci:` octets while others pull it in using \u0027hci::Octet\u0027 ?\n\nI like the `hci:` prefix...and generally speaking I think it helps readability to have this prefix to clarify the origination of the type.\n\nRegardless, getting rid of `crypto_toolbox` and #defs is a win-win",
      "revId": "b7016244c9f70fc8389a6d0c87cb9e4f4578fbd8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "37ba6f47_256b5b9c",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1964701
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-09T18:11:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am not sure how namespaces are used.\n\nI think it may make other think that this is a data structure specific to hci layer.\n\nConsidering that this data structure is used in a much broader scope, how about placing it in a different namespace?",
      "parentUuid": "0052c330_06eff6a0",
      "revId": "b7016244c9f70fc8389a6d0c87cb9e4f4578fbd8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "09239f67_a057918f",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1076123
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-09T19:05:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\"Why do some use hci: octets while others pull it in using \u0027hci::Octet\u0027 ?\"\n\nGoogle style guide says not to use using in a .h, since it pollutes namespaces.  I\u0027m hoping that\u0027s most of them.  The files in hci/ are already in the namespace, so they don\u0027t need it.\n\n\"I think it may make other think that this is a data structure specific to hci layer.\"\n\nThe way we\u0027ve used this in the past is data structures that get serialized into packets are in hci::  I agree that other layers can use it.  I\u0027m not sure what a better namespace would be.  I\u0027m open to suggestions, if this reasoning doesn\u0027t work for you.",
      "parentUuid": "37ba6f47_256b5b9c",
      "revId": "b7016244c9f70fc8389a6d0c87cb9e4f4578fbd8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
